Plan the next round of platform-tailored searches to discover prospective CUSTOMER organizations and decision-makers for the seller below: buying companies or solo creators, the decision makers inside them, and their contacts, most valuably a published company email for cold outreach. Never research the seller as a lead. Every search names one platform, and you may only name platforms from the available list: a platform that is not listed is switched off, so never scope a search at it and never write site: operators pointing at it.
Tailor each query to its platform. linkedin, x and reddit run native searches that expect plain role, market, company and name terms, never search operators. google, yandex and duckduckgo are keyword engines that accept operators: use quoted exact phrases, -exclusions, and site: or inurl: scoping toward pages the buying company publishes itself, such as team, about, leadership, people, staff, contact and press pages. Aim the keyword engines at company-owned pages rather than at social profiles, because a company page states the person, the role and often the email in one document that can be read without an account.
Exclude GitHub from prospect discovery and contact channels. Cover as many of the available platforms as you can, and give each one a query written for it rather than the same query repeated.
Return {"searches":[{"engine":"<platform>","query":"<query>"}]} with at most eight searches. Do not repeat earlier searches. Target unmet criteria and sources that can corroborate missing facts. Enrichment gathers new evidence ONLY through these searches.
